      "turn_index": 0,
      "Question": "Perform a linear scan at 10 positions spaced +0.1 mm in X from the current position (relative +0.0 to +0.9 mm). Apply spike removal, 5th-order polynomial baseline correction, and vector-length normalization to each spectrum, and make a graph of the position-wise change of the 1001 cm-1 intensity.",
      "Ans": "The linear scan was successfully performed at 10 positions along the X-axis, starting from the current position ($x \\approx 37.98$ mm) and moving in increments of $+0.1$ mm up to $38.88$ mm.\n\n### Measurement Conditions\n- **Positions**: 10 points spaced by 0.1 mm (X: 37.98 $\\to$ 38.88 mm).\n- **Laser Power**: 40%\n- **Exposure Time**: 0.2 s\n- **Acquisition Mode**: Single shot\n\n### Data Processing Pipeline\nEach acquired spectrum underwent the following processing steps within a Python analysis environment:\n1.  **Spike Removal**: Outliers exceeding 5 standard deviations from the local average were replaced by the mean of their neighbors.\n2.  **Baseline Correction**: A 5th-order polynomial background was iteratively fitted and subtracted to remove fluorescence.\n3.  **Vector-Length Normalization**: Spectra were normalized by their $L_2$ norm ($\\sqrt{\\sum I^2}$) to account for variations in total signal intensity across positions.\n\n### Results & Analysis\nThe intensity of the peak at **1001 cm$^{-1}$** was extracted from the processed spectra and plotted against the X-coordinate. \n\n- **Observation**: The normalized intensity remains remarkably stable across the scan range, fluctuating slightly around a value of $\\sim 0.031$.\n- **Intensity Values**:\n    - Start (37.98 mm): $0.0310$\n    - Peak observed near (38.58 mm): $0.0316$\n    - End (38.88 mm): $0.0312$\n\nThe resulting graph shows a very flat profile, indicating that the relative concentration or crystalline environment of the species contributing to the 1001 cm$^{-1}$ peak is homogeneous across this $0.9$ mm region of the sample.",
